KZ3 patch 1056: striped lock-line lock (64 stripes), seqlock GETLLAR, reservation hand-off under the stripe of the line it leaves, CAS kills.
Idea from NoahBPeterson/ps3recomp b709a08 (lock-line striping) and e3ab49d (seqlock GETLLAR, CAS reservation hand-off), MIT;
our own version on top of patches 1030, 1051, 1052 (keeps the atomic event_status raise/ack of 1052).
KZ3_LL_OLD=1 = one lock and the locked GETLLAR (A/B); KZ3_LL_STATS=1 = [ll-stats] every 10 s.
The upstream test_spu_lockline_peer.c ack case now races ack against raise (the ack no longer takes the lock).
Host tests: tools/spu/test_lockline.sh (with tools/spu/test_lockline_stress.c).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): coherency registry kept as our atomic array (lock-free walks under the striped lock), PR290 list not used in this file, upstream waiter wake kept.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.17.0 (SPU pass 95): #381's weak ppu_resv_break_line and its call at the top of both notify functions kept.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): ours (striped seqlock lock line) over c9a450d8 (lock-free GETLLAR for registered holders) and the list registry; upstream's bitmap pointer `g_spu_coh_bits` is now published by our reserve (the PPU store paths test it inline, spu_coh_bitmap.h; both store macros use `spu_coh_line_reserved`); upstream's line watches (`spu_coh_watch_add`, used by SPURS task signal waits 2913a317) kept and woken from our notifiers; #522's stwcx/stdcx re-check under the lock kept, under the line's stripe; upstream `spu_coh_reserve_fast` left dead (coh_listed never set).

